--!strict
--[[
	enemy/Boar/Charge: the Charger's attack (enemies.luau FrenzyBoar: windUp 0.6, strike 0.5,
	recovery 1.2). Section 9: a 0.6 s crouch, then a straight-line rush that turns slowly.

	  0.00-0.60  Anticipation: the stamp and the coil. The forelegs come up and stamp down braced
	             wide ahead, the head drops with the tusks forward and the tail flags up; the weight
	             rocks back over the haunches and holds there, trembling, for the whole wind-up.
	             A low coil: the back stays near level so all four legs read from the side, and
	             the head hangs low between the forelegs, the snout just off the field, so the
	             launch tosses it up through more than two studs. Readable from the front (the
	             lowered tusks, the braced forelegs) and from behind (the raised tail, the rear
	             sunk back). Every foot stays where it stands.
	  0.60-0.65  Snap: the launch. It springs off its haunches into the air, stretched flat, head
	             and tusks up, the forelegs reaching and the hind legs fired back.
	  0.65-0.70  Hold: held in the air.
	  0.70-1.67  the rush: the server carries the body (RushWorld.distanceAt: 28 studs a second to
	             the strike beat at 1.10, then the skid over the rest of the 22 studs, at rest at
	             1.67). The boar gallops on it: the forelegs land first, then the hind legs, a
	             suspension between; every planted foot rolls heel to toe and holds its place on
	             the field at the speed the body travels, the body rocking over each pair. The
	             strides shorten as the skid sheds the speed and it stops braced on its forelegs.
	  0.60-1.20  hit window: opens on the launch snap with the trail and stays open through the rush
	             to the tusks (the server resolves the Charger's line at windUp + strike = 1.10 s)
	  1.20-2.30  Recovery: braced, it hops its forelegs back under it, snorts and shakes its head,
	             steps its hind legs up and settles into the idle. The server turns the body.
	Generated: dense keys (one a frame) through the run, solved for the rig's rigid legs
	(rigs.luau Boar: hips 1.8 above the field, legs 1.8 x 0.8). Rig: Boar. Root X- pitches the
	nose down; Neck X- lowers the head; Hip X+ swings a leg forward; TailJoint X- lifts the tail.
]]
local Types = require(script.Parent.Parent.Parent.Parent.types)

local function rot(x: number, y: number, z: number): Types.JointKey
	return { rot = { x, y, z } }
end

local function posRot(px: number, py: number, pz: number, rx: number, ry: number, rz: number): Types.JointKey
	return { pos = { px, py, pz }, rot = { rx, ry, rz } }
end

